- **scenario**: `FaqItem.astro:7,16` renders `<div class="faq-answer">{renderedAnswer}</div>` where `renderedAnswer` is returned by `renderMarkdown()` via `markHTMLString(code)` (`src/lib/markdown.ts:29`). Astro does not add its component-scoping `[data-astro-cid-*]` attribute to elements inside `markHTMLString` output, yet `FaqItem.astro:76-102,151-157` uses unscoped descendant selectors (`.faq-answer p`, `.faq-answer p + p`, `.faq-answer ul`, `.faq-answer ol`, `.faq-answer li`, `.faq-answer a`, `.faq-answer a:hover`, and `@media (forced-colors: active) { .faq-answer a }`). Astro compiles these to `.faq-answer[data-astro-cid-...] p[data-astro-cid-...]`, so none of the 8 rules match the rendered DOM: `<p>` retains browser-default `1em` top/bottom margins instead of `margin: 0`, lists lose their spacing, and links lose both their `var(--accent)` styling and their `LinkText` forced-colors override.
- **fix**: Wrap the markdown-generated child selectors in `:global(...)` (matching the pattern in `src/pages/writing/[slug].astro:285-358`):
```css
